==Strategy==
While possible, it is extremely difficult to tackle this stage head-on. The deadly combination of Sir Metal Seal and Hackey requires good unit deploy timing from the player and RNG procs on critters and CC units such as [[Hoop Cat (Rare Cat)|Hoopmaster Cat]] or [[Volley Cat (Rare Cat)|Curry cat]]. Should you fail to defeat the horrifying duo in time, even more annoying peons, such as Dark Otters and Gory variants, appear. Even if you manage to perma-CC Sir Metal Seal, it is still nigh-impossible to stack a decent amount of attackers to deal with enemies, and 100 seconds into the battle, another Sir Metal Seal and Hackey appear, ready to wreck your offense.

Thankfully, it is possible to cheese the stage. Both threats appear on timer, and Those Guys provide a lot of money to work with.

A good Money UP combo is almost required, such as [[Offshore Accounts (Combo)|Offshore Accounts]] or [[Crazy Hearts (Combo)|Crazy Hearts]]. When the battle starts, immediately send out [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] and he will kill the first few Those Guys, giving you plenty of cash. Send out [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] as soon as you can, followed by [[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Green Shell Cat]] to give you more time to kill the base even if Sir Metal Seal spawns. Afterwards, spamming [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] and [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] will also help to rush down the base in time. Iron Wall Cannon may also be required if your Green Shell isn't sufficiently leveled up, combined with a Starting Cannon L Combo.

